# Sanity conventions

**Canonical doc:** `sanity/CLAUDE.md` — read before schema or query changes.

## Registering schemas

1. Define in `sanity/schemas/<kind>/<name>.ts` with `defineType` / `defineField`
2. Import into `sanity.config.ts` → `schema.types`
3. Singletons: also add to `singletonPlugin([...])` and `pageStructure([...])`
4. Run `npm run typegen`

## Client-friendly schemas (required)

- Every field needs a `description` in plain English
- Use field `groups` on complex documents
- Validation: `.error()` / `.warning()` with reasons, not bare `.required()`
- Limit portable-text decorators/annotations; renderer is `components/CustomPortableText.tsx`

## Queries

- All queries in `sanity/lib/queries.ts` use `defineQuery` from `next-sanity`
- Singleton: `*[_type == "home"][0]{...}`; slug filter: `$slug` param, not string interpolation
- After schema/query changes: `npm run typegen`

## Fetching

- **`sanityFetch`** for request-time reads (live revalidation + draft mode)
- `<SanityLive />` in `app/(personal)/layout.tsx` — one copy, don't move to pages
- Token via `sanity/lib/token.ts` (`server-only`); never expose to client

## New URL-backed document types

Update `sanity/plugins/resolve.ts` (`mainDocuments`, `locations`) and `resolveHref` in `sanity/lib/utils.ts`.

## Media Library

Before uploads or tag changes, read `brand-identity/asset-tagging-strategy.md`.
